\f0\b\fs24 \cf2 \cb3 Chapter 1\'a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 And the Word of the LORD came to Jonah the son of Amittai, saying, 
\f0\b 2\'a0
\f1\b0 \'93Get up! Go to the great city Nineveh and cry out against her, because their evil has come up to my face
\fs16\fsmilli8000 \super 1
\fs24 \nosupersub .\'94 
\f0\b 3\'a0
\f1\b0 But Jonah got up to flee toward Tarshish away from the face of the LORD. And he went down 
\f2\i to
\f1\i0  Joppa and found a merchant ship going to Tarshish, and paid her fare, and went on board her to go with them toward Tarshish away from the face of the LORD.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 4\'a0
\f1\b0 And the LORD hurled a great wind upon the sea, and it was a great storm surge on the sea, and the merchant ship threatened to break up. 
\f0\b 5\'a0
\f1\b0 And the mariners feared, and each cried out to his god. And they hurled the stuff that was in the merchant ship into the sea to lighten it for them. Meanwhile Jonah went down into the belly of the vessel and lay down and fell asleep and was snoring. 
\f0\b 6\'a0
\f1\b0 And the captain of the ship approached him and said to him, \'93Why are you in a deep sleep? Get up! Call on your god! Perhaps your god will take notice of us and we won\'92t perish!\'94 \
\

\f0\b 7\'a0
\f1\b0 And the mariners said each to another, \'93Come, let us cast lots so that we may know on whose account this disaster has come on us!\'94 And they cast lots, and the lot fell on Jonah. 
\f0\b 8\'a0
\f1\b0 So they said to him, \'93Please tell us whoever is responsible that this disaster has come upon us! What is your occupation? And from where do you come? What is your country? And from which people are you?\'94 
\f0\b 9\'a0
\f1\b0 And he said to them, \'93I am a Hebrew, a slave of the LORD, and I fear the LORD, the God of heaven, who made the sea and the dry land.\'94 
\f0\b 10\'a0
\f1\b0 Then the men feared with great fear, and they said to him, \'93What is this you have done?\'94 because they knew that he was fleeing from the face of the LORD (because he had told them). \
\

\f0\b 11\'a0
\f1\b0 So they said to him, \'93What shall we do to you so that the sea may quiet down for us?\'94 because the sea was growing more and more tempestuous. 
\f0\b 12\'a0
\f1\b0 And he said to them, \'93Pick me up and hurl me into the sea so that the sea may quiet down for you, because I know that I am responsible that this great storm has come upon you all.\'94 
\f0\b 13\'a0
\f1\b0 But the men rowed hard
\fs16\fsmilli8000 \super 2
\fs24 \nosupersub  to bring the ship back to the dry land, and they could not do so because the sea was growing more and more tempestuous against them. 
\f0\b 14\'a0
\f1\b0 So they cried out to the LORD, and they said, \'93O LORD! Please do not let us perish because of this man\'92s life, and do not make us guilty of innocent blood, because you, O LORD, did what you wanted.\'94 
\f0\b 15\'a0
\f1\b0 And they picked Jonah up and hurled him into the sea, and the sea ceased from its raging. 
\f0\b 16\'a0
\f1\b0 So the men feared the LORD greatly, and they offered a sacrifice to the LORD and made vows.\
\

\f0\b Chapter 2
\f1\b0  \
(
\f0\b 1.17)\'a0
\f1\b0 And the LORD appointed a large sea monster to swallow up Jonah, and Jonah was in the belly of the beast three days and three nights.\

\f0\b 2 
\f1\b0 And Jonah prayed to the LORD his God from the belly of the sea monster 
\f0\b 3\'a0
\f1\b0 and said,\
\
\'93I called from my distress to the LORD,\uc0\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0and he answered me;\u8232 from the belly of Sheol I cried for help\'97\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0you heard my voice.\

\f0\b 4
\f1\b0  And you threw me into the deep,\uc0\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0into the heart of the seas,\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0and the sea currents surrounded me;\u8232 all your breakers and your surging waves\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0passed over me.
\f0\b \
5
\f1\b0  And I said, \'91I am banished\uc0\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0from your sight;\u8232 how will I continue to look\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0on your holy temple?\'92
\f0\b \
6\'a0
\f1\b0 The waters encompassed me up to my neck;\uc0\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0the deep surrounded me;\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0seaweed was wrapped around my head.\

\f0\b 7\'a0
\f1\b0 I went down to the foundations of the mountains;\uc0\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0the Underworld\'97its bars were around me forever.\u8232 But you brought up my life from the pit,\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0O LORD my God.\

\f0\b 8\'a0
\f1\b0 When my life was ebbing away from me,\uc0\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0I remembered the LORD,\u8232 and my prayer came to you,\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0to your holy temple.
\f0\b \
9\'a0
\f1\b0 Those who worship vain idols\uc0\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0forsake their loyal love.
\f0\b \
10\'a0
\f1\b0 But I, with a voice of thanksgiving,\uc0\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0will sacrifice to you;\u8232 I will fulfill what I have vowed.\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0Salvation belongs to the LORD!\'94\

\f0\b \
11\'a0
\f1\b0 And the LORD spoke to the fish, and it vomited Jonah out on the dry land.\
\

\f0\b Chapter 3\'a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 And the Word of the LORD came to Jonah a second time, saying, 
\f0\b 2\'a0
\f1\b0 \'93Get up! Go to Nineveh, the great city, and proclaim to it the message that I am telling you.\'94 
\f0\b 3\'a0
\f1\b0 So Jonah got up and went to Nineveh according to the Word of the LORD. \
\
Now Nineveh was an extraordinarily great city\'97a journey of three days. 
\f0\b 4\'a0
\f1\b0 And Jonah began to go into the city a journey of one day, and he cried out and said, \'93Forty
\fs16\fsmilli8000 \super 3
\fs24 \nosupersub  more days and Nineveh will be overturned!\'94 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 5\'a0
\f1\b0 And the people of Nineveh believed in God, and they proclaimed a fast and put on sackcloth\'97from the greatest of them to the least. 
\f0\b 6\'a0
\f1\b0 And the news reached the king of Nineveh, and he rose from his throne and removed his royal robe, put on sackcloth, and sat in the ashes. 
\f0\b 7\'a0
\f1\b0 And he had a proclamation made, and said, \'93In Nineveh, by a decree of the king and his nobles: \'93No human being or animal, no herd or flock, shall taste anything! They must not eat, and they must not drink water! 
\f0\b 8\'a0
\f1\b0 And the human beings and the animals must be covered with sackcloth! And they must call forcefully to God, and each must turn from his evil way and from the violence that is in his hands. 
\f0\b 9\'a0
\f1\b0 Who knows? God may relent and change his mind and turn from his blazing anger so that we will not perish.\'94 
\f0\b 10\'a0
\f1\b0 And God saw their deeds\'97that they turned from their evil ways\'97and God changed his mind about the evil that he had said he would bring upon them, and he did not do it.\
\

\f0\b Chapter 4\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 And this was evil to Jonah, a great evil, and he became blazingly angry. 
\f0\b 2\'a0
\f1\b0 And he prayed to the LORD and said, \'93O LORD, were these not my words while I was in my homeland? Therefore I had the foresight to flee to Tarshish, because I knew that you are a gracious and compassionate God, slow to anger and having great steadfast love, and one who relents concerning calamity. 
\f0\b 3\'a0
\f1\b0 And so then, O LORD, please take my life from me, because for me death is better than life!\'94 
\f0\b 4\'a0
\f1\b0 And the LORD said, \'93Is it right for you to be blazingly angry?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\i\fs22 \cf2 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\b\fs24 \cf2 \cb3 5\'a0
\f1\b0 And Jonah went out from the city and sat down east of the city, and he made for himself a shelter there. And he sat under it in the shade, waiting to see what would happen with the city. 
\f0\b 6\'a0
\f1\b0 And the LORD God appointed a plant, and he made it grow up over Jonah to be a shade over his head, to save
\fs16\fsmilli8000 \super 4
\fs24 \nosupersub  him from his misery. And Jonah rejoiced with great joy about the plant. \
\

\f0\b 7\'a0
\f1\b0 So God appointed a worm at daybreak the next day, and it attacked the plant, and it withered. 
\f0\b 8\'a0
\f1\b0 And when the sun rose, God appointed a scorching east wind, and the sun attacked Jonah\'92s head and he grew faint. And he asked that he could die and said, \'93My death is better than my life!\'94 
\f0\b 9\'a0
\f1\b0 So God said to Jonah, \'93Is it right for you to be blazingly angry about the plant?\'94 And he said, \'93It is right for me to be blazingly angry enough to die!\'94\
\

\f0\b 10\'a0
\f1\b0 But the LORD said, \'93You are troubled about the plant, for which you did not labor nor cause it to grow. It grew up in a night and it perished in a night! 
\f0\b 11\'a0
\f1\b0 And should I not be concerned about Nineveh, the great city, in which there are more than one hundred and twenty thousand people who do not know right from left, plus many animals?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

